{"event_id": "evt_0018", "session": 1, "turn_no": 1, "world_time": "Sandbox, night", "actor": "gm", "kind": "gm_narration", "summary": "Narration for amw8fgc2etj9nea.", "visibility": "player", "knowledge_type": "fact", "known_to": [], "caused_by": [], "roll_ids": [], "tags": [], "details": {"text": "You slide the blaster into its holster. Your left hand is empty now; the blade hums in your right.\n\n\"Wick. Is something shut in there? Tell me what you know.\"\n\nHe doesn't have to think about it. \"Tools. Just tools, the crew said. They were going to open it again when the Warden said so. Nothing in there but tools.\"\n\nThe indigo blade goes through the chain in one pass. Sparks jump across the gravel and the yard flares violet for a heartbeat; the cut links ring off the hasp, loud in the quiet. You haul the door open. Wick lifts the lantern past your shoulder and the light finds shelves, a workbench, coils of hose. Tools.\n\nYou set your weight to step inside.\n\nSomething hits you from the left before you hear it. A dog the size of a man, heavy in the chest, jaws already open, comes out of the dark between the silos and closes on your left forearm. The teeth go deep. You feel them grate, feel the shake of its head, and the arm goes hot and then strangely far away. Blood runs off your fingers and spatters the doorstep. Your vision narrows to a bright tunnel; the lantern light swings as Wick stumbles back with a thin cry.\n\nThe dog lets go and gathers itself at your left, an arm's length away, its muzzle dark and wet in the lantern light. Wick is two steps behind you. The shed doorway is at your back, the shelves of tools behind it. The yard beyond the light is black.\n\nYour forearm is torn open and bleeding freely. You are still on your feet, the blade still lit in your right hand.\n\nYou are faster. What do you do?\n"}, "idempotency_key": "amw8fgc2etj9nea:narr"}
